# docs/README-claims.waived — claims a document may make without the token existing in a clone.
#
# One token per line, no reasons here: the reason belongs in the document that names it and in
# the commit that added the line (Rule 27). Anything not listed here must resolve.
#
# The live schedule and the fleet-sync map are the OPERATOR'S, in the hoard: a clone ships the
# .example forms only. A page may name the live path because that is where a user will find it.
config/cron.yaml
config/tailscale-sync.yaml
# ── files a SEAT writes at runtime (the tree ships only their .example forms, or nothing)
config/backend
config/crew-harness
config/secondmate-harness
config/Eindri-home-harness
config/herdr-presentation-spaces
config/trace-context
config/x-mode.env
config/fleet.json
config/grants.yaml
config/model-catalog.yaml
